      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "After updating to 22.11.2 video players no longer crash VRChat, however video feeds of most video players have issues properly displaying visuals. Sometimes the video behaves normally, but about 80% of the time a video will loop half a second's worth of footage for 3 to 6 seconds, then update to where the video should be and continue looping again from that point. It's very jarring to watch, and re-syncing a video player does not fix it. Audio does not de-sync at all in this way.\n\nEdit: Backpatching my AMD drivers to 22.4.2 fixes the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
