      "value": "@{6237e4278e32e55276d9888e|full_name}: It was video feed stuttering of a sort yes. Normally I'd expect a stutter to hang on a particular frame and then either desync a little bit or catch up to where it should be, but this was much more visually aggressive. The stutter was present in every video I had attempted to view, though I don't know if it would occur with something like a twitch stream. The stutters weren't consistent in when they would occur or duration, but a video couldn't go 10 seconds straight without at least one happening. Rather than being merely annoying they were unwatchable for me. If I weren't as acclimated to VR as I am it probably would have been nauseating. I attempted a reinstall of both VRChat and a clean install of the most recent AMD driver on the day I made the above comment to no avail. I have not experienced this stuttering at all since setting my drivers back to AMD 22.4.2.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
